Question: {"question": "What does Boulder do this round?", "consider": ["Its nature, traits, likes, dislikes, mood and impressions in `monsters.e0`", "What happened to it this round in `monsters.e0.this_round`", "Which side the other monsters are on in `group`", "What the party did and said in `party`"]}
Options:
(A) attack: {"what": "Attack one member of the party", "when": "It is hostile or angry at the party, or the party just attacked it"}
(B) special: {"what": "Use its special attack: bring down a rockslide on the whole party", "when": "It is hostile and wants to hit hard"}
(C) defend: {"what": "Brace and guard itself instead of acting", "when": "It is badly hurt or expects a heavy blow and wants to wait it out"}
(D) flee: {"what": "Run away from the fight", "when": "It is scared or badly hurt, or the other monsters have turned against it"}
(E) converse: {"what": "Talk instead of fighting this round", "when": "It is curious or undecided and wants to answer or chat rather than act"}
(F) demand_tribute: {"what": "Demand gold from the party in exchange for not fighting", "when": "It is greedy and sees a chance to get paid"}
(G) leave_peacefully: {"what": "End its part in the encounter peacefully and let the party go on its way", "when": "It has no quarrel with the party and would rather go"}
